# Credentials. Not tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Working state. Not a deliverable.
#
# **Sharing it breaks things.** current-work-item.json is "the work item I have started right now,"
# and if shared, whoever clones it starts out working on someone else's work item.
# Their records get linked to someone else's work item. cursors are this machine's per-session
# read positions and mean nothing elsewhere.
#
# **Its absence does not pass silently.** If a record is produced without the marker, it is kept
# in telemetry/unattributed.jsonl with the reason, and the checks report the count.
.autodrive/

# A place for humans to use. **Its contents are not tracked.**
#
# **Only the README is tracked.** Ignoring everything would make the directory itself disappear
# in a clone, and with it "what must not be put here".
notes/*
!notes/README.md

# Core dumps. **Not tracked.**
#
# Produced when tests crash. They contain the runtime memory as-is, so **environment variable values
# are included in plain text.** A 39MB core dump was actually committed with credentials in it
# (AUT-137). Being binary, most secret-scanning tools do not even scan them.
core
core.*
